@startuml
title Internal role migration

skinparam sequenceFontSize 14

participant "DBaaS Operator" as Operator
participant "DBaaS Aggregator" as Aggregator
database "Registry" as Registry
participant "DBaaS Adapter" as Adapter

note over Aggregator
  Started by the registration process. The physical database
  row keeps its old values until completion.
end note

Aggregator -> Registry: acquire the keep-alive lock\nroles-migration-{phydbid}-{type}
note right: while the lock is held, every registration\nof this physical database answers 202

loop while a logical database still lacks a required role
  Aggregator -> Registry: next portion of logical databases\nmissing at least one required role
  loop per logical database
    Aggregator -> Aggregator: missed roles =\nrequired - existing
    loop per missed role
      Aggregator -> Adapter: PUT {address}/api/v2/dbaas/adapter/{type}/users\n(dbName, role)
      Adapter --> Aggregator: 201: connection properties\nand resources
    end
  end

  alt a user creation failed
    Aggregator -> Registry: store the failure\n(database id, message) in the instruction
    note over Aggregator: the migration stops;\nthe failure stays in the instruction,\nthe lock is released
  end

  Aggregator -> Registry: save the connection properties of the migrated databases,\ndrop the stored failures of the migrated databases,\nsave the instruction
end

group @Transactional
  Aggregator -> Registry: apply the parked registration request,\ndelete the instruction
  Aggregator -> Aggregator: reset the adapter and\nphysical database caches
end
Aggregator -> Registry: release the lock

note over Operator, Aggregator
  The operator learns the outcome on its next registration:
  lock held - 202; stored failures of a previous run - 500
  (and the migration restarts); after completion - 200.
end note
@enduml
